<Section title="Thermal Loading" id="thermal_loading"></Section>

<SubSection title="Thermal Effects: Temperature Changes" id="thermal_effects_temperature_changes">

<strong>Notation</strong>
<ul> 
     <li>  <InlineEquation equation='\\Delta T > 0, \\sigma < 0' /> : Compression</li> 
     <li>   <InlineEquation equation='\\Delta T < 0, \\sigma > 0' /> : Tension</li> 
</ul> 

<p>
    <InlineEquation equation='\\delta_T' /> ,  <InlineEquation equation='\\varepsilon_T' />  present in addition to elastic  <InlineEquation equation='\\delta_E' /> ,  <InlineEquation equation='\\varepsilon_E' />  (from internal forces). Superposition (small strains):
 <DisplayEquation equation='\\varepsilon_{tot} = \\varepsilon_{E} + \\varepsilon_{T}\\' title="Total strain." background="True" /> 
  <DisplayEquation equation='\\delta_{tot} = \\delta_{E} + \\delta_{T}\\' title="Total displacement." background="True" /> 
</p>

<Image src='/sol/axial_loading/Temperature_NoLoad.png' width='4'>Temperature changes with no applied loads</Image>

 A rod rests freely on a smooth horizontal surface. Temperature of the rod is raised by <InlineEquation equation='\\Delta T' />. Rod elongates by an amount.

<DisplayEquation equation='\\delta_{T} = \\alpha \\Delta T L\\' title="Displacement from temperature changes." background="True" />

 Linear coefficient of thermal expansion <InlineEquation equation='\\alpha' />,  <InlineEquation equation='[\\alpha] = \\frac{1}{K},\\frac{1}{°C},...' />. This deformation is associated with an average thermal strain:

<DisplayEquation equation='\\varepsilon_{T} = \\frac{\\delta_T}{L} = \\alpha T\\' title="Strain from temperature changes." background="True" />

<Image src='/sol/axial_loading/Temperature_TwoPlates.png' width='1.5'>  
    Temperature changes with statically indeterminate beam
</Image>

 Initially, rod of length <InlineEquation equation='L' /> is placed between two supports at a distance <InlineEquation equation='L' /> from each other. With no internal forces, there is no stress or strain.

<DisplayEquation equation='R_{A} = R_{B} = 0\\' title="Force balance." background="True" />
<DisplayEquation equation='R_{A} = F\\' title="Reaction force." background="True" />
                  
 After raising the temperature, total elongation of the rod is still zero. The total elongation is given by:

<DisplayEquation equation='\\delta = \\frac{FL}{EA} + \\alpha L \\Delta T = 0\\' title="Total elongation." background="True" />

 The stress in the rod due to change in temperature is given by:
<DisplayEquation equation='\\sigma = -\\alpha E \\Delta T\\' title="Stress from temperature changes." background="True"  />

</SubSection>

